      "widgets_values": [
        "## RefMod A/B/C · A: the latent tail only\n\nIssues #7 and #8: does a RefMod built from an early chunk bring a place back later without dragging its composition along? Variant **A** is the baseline: Orrery Continue carries the last 22 frames from clip to clip, and nothing else remembers the salon.\n\n1. Generate ×4 plays the tour (segments 0 to 3) into `output/abc_a/`.\n2. After segment 0 exists, copy it to B and C: `python experiments/refmod-abc/copy_segment0.py <ComfyUI output folder>`.\n\nOrrery Refs is wired only into the preview, so every variant gets the same prompt: the SEND: stills show up there without reaching Reference to Video. The lint \"Reference to Video has 0 wired\" is expected. Scoring: `experiments/refmod-abc/run_sheet.md`."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## RefMod A/B/C · A: the latent tail only\n\nIssues #7 and #8: does a RefMod built from an early chunk bring a place back later without dragging its composition along? Variant **A** is the baseline: Orrery Continue carries the last 22 frames from clip to clip, and nothing else remembers the salon.\n\n1. Generate ×4 plays the tour (segments 0 to 3) into `output/abc_a/`.\n2. After segment 0 exists, copy it to B and C: `python experiments/refmod-abc/copy_segment0.py <ComfyUI output folder>`.\n\nOrrery Refs is wired only into the preview, so every variant gets the same prompt: the SEND: stills show up there without reaching Reference to Video. The lint \"Reference to Video has 0 wired\" is expected. Scoring: `experiments/refmod-abc/run_sheet.md`."
      },
